# Delete workspaces

`--delete` resolves a discovered named-workspace session, forgets and removes
its checkout, then closes it when live.

    :bins jj tmux cat test

> [!NOTE]
> 'jj', 'tmux', 'cat', and 'test' are available.

    :copy tests/fixtures/jjconfig.toml .jjconfig.toml (copied)

    :t rename-session -t 0 runner (success)
    :$ jj git init alpha (exit: 0)
    :$ jj workspace add -R alpha --name feature alpha.feature (exit: 0)
    :$ jj workspace add -R alpha --name other alpha.other (exit: 0)

Create a plain collision and a disambiguated repo-backed feature session. Strict
metadata should ensure deletion closes only the latter.

    :t new-session -d -s alpha/feature "cat" (success)
    :t new-session -d -s alpha/feature~1 -c alpha.feature "cat" (success)
    :t set-option -F -t '=alpha/feature~1:' @smth.repo '#{pane_current_path}' (success)
    :t new-session -d -s scratch "cat" (success)

    :$ smth --base alpha --delete feature (exit: 0)
    :t has-session -t '=alpha/feature~1' (failure)

```
can't find session: alpha/feature~1
```

    :t has-session -t '=alpha/feature' (success)
    :$ test ! -e alpha.feature (exit: 0)

A discovered workspace without a live tmux session should still be forgotten
and removed through the same session operation.

    :$ smth --base alpha --repo "alpha*" --delete other (exit: 0)
    :$ test ! -e alpha.other (exit: 0)

Only the default workspace should remain registered.

    :$ jj workspace list -R alpha --ignore-working-copy --no-pager --color never --template 'name ++ "\n"' (exit: 0)

```stdout
default
```

Missing sessions and the default checkout are not deletable.

    :$ smth --base alpha --delete missing (exit: 1)

```stderr
error: session not found
```

    :$ smth --base alpha --repo "alpha*" --delete default (exit: 1)

```stderr
error: session not found
```

    :$ test -d alpha (exit: 0)

Delete rejects the plain-session namespace and never closes a same-named plain
session on an invalid request.

    :$ smth --no-base --delete scratch (exit: 1)

```stderr
error: session cannot be deleted
```

    :t has-session -t '=scratch' (success)

The operand is mandatory, picker controls are rejected, and delete is mutually
exclusive with every other lifecycle action.

    :$ smth --base alpha --delete (exit: 2)

```stderr
error: a value is required for '--delete <SESSION>' but none was supplied

For more information, try 'help'.
```

    :$ smth --base alpha --delete missing --query missing (exit: 2)

```stderr
error: the argument '--delete <SESSION>' cannot be used with '--query <STR>'

Usage: smth --base <REPO> --delete <SESSION>

For more information, try 'help'.
```

    :$ smth --base alpha --delete missing --close missing (exit: 2)

```stderr
error: the argument '--delete <SESSION>' cannot be used with '--close [<SESSION>]'

Usage: smth --base <REPO> --delete <SESSION>

For more information, try 'help'.
```

